.TH SPACEGL-SERVER 1 "2026-04-19" "SpaceGL @VERSION@" "SpaceGL Manual"
.SH NAME
spacegl-server \- SpaceGL galaxy server launcher script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spacegl-server
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spacegl-server
is a Bash wrapper script that provides an interactive startup interface
for the SpaceGL galaxy server. It displays the SpaceGL banner, asks for
the master key interactively when the
.B SPACEGL_KEY
environment variable is not already set, and then delegates execution
to
.BR spacegl_server (1)
(looked up as
.IR ./build/spacegl_server ,
then
.IR ./spacegl_server ,
then in
.BR PATH ).
.PP
All arguments passed to this script are forwarded verbatim to the
underlying
.B spacegl_server
binary.
.PP
On its first boot the server creates its own identity key,
.IR [DATA\-DIR]/server_identity.key ,
and prints its fingerprint ("Server identity CREATED ... SHA256:...");
on every later boot it prints "Server identity loaded". The decks pin
this identity (wire revision 4): back the file up together with the data
directory, or every deck that has met the server will refuse it as a
changed server.
.SH OPTIONS
Any option accepted by
.BR spacegl_server (1)
is passed through unchanged, in particular:
.TP
.B \-\-data\-dir DIR
Root directory of the persistent state (galaxy.dat, captains/,
server_identity.key).
.TP
.B \-\-print\-identity
Print the server's fingerprint and the 64 hex digits of its public key
(for
.B SPACEGL_SERVER_KEY
on the decks) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-io=MODE
.B legacy
(default) or
.B async
event loop.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SPACEGL_KEY
If set, the master key prompt is skipped and this value is used directly.
.TP
.B SPACEGL_KEY_FILE
Read by
.BR spacegl_server (1):
a file holding the master key (64 hex digits, mode 0600). The script
still asks for a key when
.B SPACEGL_KEY
is not set; with a key file, export
.B SPACEGL_KEY
or start
.B spacegl_server
directly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I [DATA\-DIR]/server_identity.key
The server's identity (private key, mode 0600).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
export SPACEGL_KEY="$(openssl rand \-hex 32)"
\&./spacegl\-server
\&./spacegl\-server \-\-print\-identity
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spacegl_server (1),
.BR spacegl-client (1),
.BR spacegl_client (1)
